2 01 18`; WriteTxFifo `00 02 d0..d3` \u2192 `04 52 00 00 00 00`.\n6 of 12 GOs used; no duplicate GO ids; no retries; no background SPI. Receipts: hd26-h-sent-<case> / hd26-h-restored-<case>.\nThe first SENT for ctl failed to post (empty body rejected by the mailbox); it was re-posted correctly from saved evidence, with no retransmission.\n\nRestoration after each of the 6 (all baseline_ok=true): clear_tx \u2192 TX level 0; FIFO flags 03/27 unchanged; sys irq 0x00000002 (FIFO_TX newly raised by the carrier) \u2192 clear_irq_status{0x2} only \u2192 0x00000000; errors 0; STBY_XOSC.\n\n## Final state (02:41:52Z)\n- Radio: irq 0x00000000, STBY_XOSC, errors 0, TX FIFO 0, FIFO flags rx 0x03 / tx 0x27. Equals the baseline.\n- spidev: mode 0 (mode32 0x0), bits 8, lsb 0, default max 8000000 Hz. App: `./mcp_radio --mcp-http` pid 7973 (Oct 7 13:02:58), not restarted.\n- Pins unchanged: GPIO4 op hi, GPIO5 ip lo, GPIO6 ip pu hi, GPIO18 ip pd lo, GPIO20 ip pd lo. No pigpiod.\n- No RF/SetTx/SetRx, GPIO/reset/config/DIO/IRQ-mask writes, helpers, dependencies, rebuilds or repo edits. **pi134 untouched.**\n- Host evidence: scratchpad/h/ (per-case JSON, sent/restore receipts, log.txt, seen_go.txt).\n",
